      "id": "claim_07801bdda3384be9a15a7f483448d507",
      "statement": "Each package's test run is a Vite+ task (not a script) so vitest scratch paths (node_modules/.vite, .vite-temp, .wrangler — excluded workspace-wide because wrangler scratch reaches past the owning package) stay out of the fingerprint; the cached vp path replays instantly for untouched packages but loses to plain vitest (test:run) on a just-edited package by more than the whole suite costs on a small one.",
      "evidence": [
